hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19708","Haddathana Hushaym, akhbarana Yala ibn Ata, from Umarah ibn Hadid, from Sakhr al-Ghamidi, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning. He said: And when he dispatched a detachment or an army, he dispatched them at the beginning of the day. He said: And Sakhr was a merchant man, and he used to send out his merchandise at the beginning of the day. He said: So he became rich and his wealth increased."
"19709","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Shubah, he said: Yala ibn Ata informed me, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Hadid, a man from Bajilah, he said: I heard Sakhr al-Ghamidi, a man from al-Azd, saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he dispatched a detachment, dispatched them at the beginning of the day. And Sakhr was a merchant man and he had servants, and he used to send his servants at the beginning of the day. He said: So his wealth increased until he did not know where to place it."
"19710","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah, from Yala ibn Ata, from Umarah ibn Hadid al-Bajali, from Sakhr al-Ghamidi, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he dispatched a detachment, dispatched it at the beginning of the day. And Sakhr was a merchant, and he would send his servants only at the beginning of the day, so his wealth increased until he did not know where to place it."
"19711","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Marwazi, he said: Haddathana Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Majishun, he said: Akhbarani Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I entered upon Jabir ibn Abd Allah while he was dying, and I said: Convey greetings from me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"19712","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Muqatil, akhbarana Abbad ibn al-Awwam, haddathana al-Hajjaj, from Abd Allah, freedman of Banu Hashim, he said: And he was trustworthy. He said: And al-Hakam used to take from him, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: He was asked about the milk of camels, and he said: Perform ablution from their milk. And he was asked about the milk of sheep, and he said: Do not perform ablution from their milk."
"19713","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Muqatil, haddathana Ibn al-Mubarak, akhbarana Misar, from Hammad, he said: Urine in our view is like blood; as long as it is not the size of a dirham, there is no harm in it."
